==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm}} {{term|bawlen|lang=enm}}, from {{etyl|non}} {{term|baula||to low|lang=non}} and/or {{etyl|ML.}} {{term|baulo|baulō|bark|pos=verb|lang=la}}, both from {{proto|Germanic|title=Proto Germanic base|bau-|to roar|lang=en}}, from {{proto|Indo-European|to bark|lang=en}}, conflated with {{proto|Germanic|bellanan|to roar|lang=en}}, from {{proto|Indo-European|bʰel-|to sound, roar|lang=en}}. Cognate with {{etyl|is|-}} {{term|baula||to moo, low|lang=is}}, {{etyl|sv|-}} {{term|böla||to bellow, low|lang=sv}}. More at {{l|en|bell}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/bɔːl/}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|/bɔl/}}
* {{a|cot-caught}} {{IPA|/bɑl/}}
* {{rhymes|ɔːl}}
* {{homophones|ball}}<!--perhaps not in all dialects but in Australian English and in New York City-->

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{intransitive}} To [[shout]] or [[utter]] in a loud and [[intense]] manner.
# {{intransitive}} To [[wail]]; to give out a [[blaring]] [[cry]].

